{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1462451-how-might-a-group-of-mages-help-a-changeling-at-risk-of-being-undone-by-banality","id":1462451,"title":"How might a group of Mages help a Changeling at risk of being Undone by Banality?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-10-02T11:36:06-07:00","id":1462451,"title":"How might a group of Mages help a Changeling at risk of being Undone by Banality?","content":"So I was considering a plot hook involving a character named <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Samhaintha\" target=\"_blank\">Doc Samhaintha</a> where she enlists the mages to help her with one of her patients. <br /> <br /> -Would she ask a group of mages for help? <br /> <br /> -Is there anything a group of mages could feasably do to help that she herself couldn't do?<br /> <br /> -I imagine them meeting at a club where Sam is partying to regain her Glamour. Would this be happening in the real world? What might that look like? Would partying with a satyr be a crazy trip to wonderland, or just partying?<br /> <br /> -What kind of problems might the players have trying to cure a changeling of their banality? I assume it wouldn't be as simple as a mind effect &quot;remove banalty&quot; but a little more involved than that. Suggestions?<br /> <br /> -Any way I could make this a little more dangerous for the PC's? <br /> <br /> -Anything I haven't considered?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-02T12:24:46-07:00","id":1462456,"title":"","content":"There isn't a canonical answer for what Mages could do here, but I think it's reasonable for suitably powerful Mages to be able to do something about Banality, although we're talking like Prime 5 + some high level of Mind level, and finding Masters like that, let alone ones willing to help you would be neither easy nor cheap.<br /> <br /> One way to make it dangerous is to have these mages not be able to do much, but maybe they could find ones that can, and getting involved with mages like that turns into something risky for all the local Kithain, like draining Freeholds for their Glamour or the like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-02T12:33:07-07:00","id":1462459,"title":"","content":"Well, assume we are talking about Arete 3 mages here. I am assuming this is going to be more than a &quot;Roll arete to remove banality Effect&quot; and probably involving the mages doing... something... to help? I am just not familiar enough with changeling to know how that all works.<br /> <br /> Mostly I found her an interesting character and wanted to see how to incorporate her into a mage chronicle, maybe as a one-off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-02T20:24:51-07:00","id":1462509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Froggy711</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1462451-how-might-a-group-of-mages-help-a-changeling-at-risk-of-being-undone-by-banality#post1462451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Would she ask a group of mages for help?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Changelings are by far the splat with less concerns about mixing up with other splats without much of a care.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Froggy711</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1462451-how-might-a-group-of-mages-help-a-changeling-at-risk-of-being-undone-by-banality#post1462451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-I imagine them meeting at a club where Sam is partying to regain her Glamour. Would this be happening in the real world?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably. It would happen in whatever place she finds better to both party and discuss, which may be in the real world, at a Freehold or in the Dreaming if she have the means to bring them there. A Freehold, probably, but some Arts let her do that. Changelings also don't care a lot about secrecy for many of their Freeholds.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Froggy711</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1462451-how-might-a-group-of-mages-help-a-changeling-at-risk-of-being-undone-by-banality#post1462451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What might that look like? Would partying with a satyr be a crazy trip to wonderland, or just partying?</div> </div> </div> </div>Party HARD. By their Birthright:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Gift of Pan</b> \u2014 When a satyr thoroughly indulges herself in<br /> one of her passions \u2014 often sexual, but also artistic and creative<br /> \u2014 those around her are also caught up in the frenzy. Fae and<br /> mortal alike join her in her dancing and debauchery. The Gift of<br /> Pan doesn\u2019t force anyone to partake in sex or any other activity,<br /> but removes inhibitions that might normally keep someone from<br /> indulging. Rather than creating a new passion, the Gift of Pan<br /> removes the barriers of social convention that might otherwise<br /> prevent someone from being able to completely surrender to an<br /> action of passion or revelry. Those failing a Banality or Willpower<br /> roll (difficulty 8) find themselves helpless to resist indulging their<br /> secret desires. </div> </div> </div>Keeping with the spirit of Changeling, make this a fun and light moment, unless your players want to explore traumatic revelations. The Gift is a fantastic tool to reveal more about a character in what have to be a safe environment for the players and usually s for the characters.<br /> <br /> Of course, Satyrs can't control but are aware of their Birthright, so she probably won't indulge (and activate the gift) if she doesn't think it will be safe and fun.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Froggy711</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1462451-how-might-a-group-of-mages-help-a-changeling-at-risk-of-being-undone-by-banality#post1462451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-What kind of problems might the players have trying to cure a changeling of their banality? I assume it wouldn't be as simple as a mind effect &quot;remove banalty&quot; but a little more involved than that. Suggestions?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the best course of action here would be to first require that they truly <i>understand</i> Banality. It is as much a mystical force as a state of mind, and understanding it would require that they interact more with the fae and the Dreaming, as long as you want them to. They'll need to study Glamour just as much, a form of Quintessence generated by creative force.<br /> <br /> They should probably have to capture and study at least one normal and one Banal chimera, with Banal chimerae being rare and very dangerous. They would have to explore the Near Dreaming a little for those. Also it would be interesting if one of them went through a Reverie, the main form of Glamour harvesting, which consists in a Changeling literally acting to inspire them for some creative act, generally artistic, but can be magical.<br /> <br /> From the Mage's perspective it would be going through the process of creating something, maybe a new rote, with a Changeling coming to visit frequently, nudging them to continue the effort with gusto, either through encouragement, manipulation, seduction, anything. It isn't a ritual and s actually a very mundane action, but is made magical by the emotional charge involved. At the end the Changeling must simply watch the final product, and the Mage will be able to witness the powerful flow of pure Quintessence that, together with the emotions involved, make this moment from mundane to transcendental.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Froggy711</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1462451-how-might-a-group-of-mages-help-a-changeling-at-risk-of-being-undone-by-banality#post1462451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Any way I could make this a little more dangerous for the PC's?</div> </div> </div> </div>Above all, interactions with the fae are emotionally charged. They're not considered as emotional vampires by some for nothing, although they can have positive relationships and feed Glamour through purely constructed ways, they never left anything they touch indifferent. They can't, otherwise... they fall to Banality, as her patient.<br /> <br /> On simpler terms, some Kiths have pretty dangerous Birthrights and dealing with Changelings will mean stay Enchanted for a long time. Enchanted people interact with Chimerae almost as completely as Changelings do, and the revelation that the world is actually full of them and they now can hurt you is pretty dangerous. The Birthrights are innate abilities of the Kiths, so they are pretty hard for Mages to counter directly as they're not &quot;magic&quot;.<br /> <br /> The Gift of Pan isn't magic. It is as part of a satyr as someone's voice or skin. To make things dangerous I recommend you to have them interacting with members of one or more of the following Kiths:<br /> <br /> - Clurichaun, they can provoke any person to fight any other person (including himself) and get away from the vicinity;<br /> - Pooka, if you have any secret whatsoever they can make you talk or greatly drain your Willpower trying not to just by talking. And they talk A LOT;<br /> - Redcap, they can bite through anything, consume anything, and literally have a maneuver to take out a limb from you with one action in combat;<br /> - Autumn Sidhe, each time they have a significant enough interaction with a PC that PC will make a Willpower roll to avoid becoming obsessed with the Sidhe;<br /> <br /> You can always resort to Changeling sorcerers and make your players deal with strange magic that they'll not know how to counter or unmake yet. You will find interesting effects that will give them a hard time in unconventional ways in Autumn, Contract, Naming and Sovereign.<br /> <br /> Finally, dealing too much with the Dreaming or staying too much time in a Freehold can affect Changelings with Bedlam. You may decide that your PCs also risk a yet unknown form of Quiet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Froggy711</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1462451-how-might-a-group-of-mages-help-a-changeling-at-risk-of-being-undone-by-banality#post1462451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Is there anything a group of mages could feasably do to help that she herself couldn't do?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. Several.<br /> <br /> - The most direct rout would be, after learning enough about what they're dealing with, to cast something to sooth and renew the patient's mind while removing the mystical side of it. I would personally use Entropy 1 (to &quot;see&quot; the Banality for what it is), Mind 2 or 3 (to read and change impulses and emotions), Prime 3 (to infuse Quintessence in the form of Glamour), Spirit 2 (to touch the fae self with the effect) and Time 2 (to bring the emotional state of their mind after their Chrysalis). Such effect would require a ton of Quintessence, though, and many successes, at least 10 Quintessence <i>per Dot</i> of permanent Banality and successes would be 1 for each Banality Dot to be removed, plus the ones needed to reach enough into the past, so bringing down a target that went the Chrysalis 15 years ago from 8 to 3 of Banality would be 8 successes.<br /> <br /> - Other interesting route is to act as their bodyguard in the Dreaming and help the patient to achieve a phenomenal Quest, as this kind of thing do help Changelings. The PCs would have as much adventure and danger as you want as they find a suitable adventure and help the Changeling at the same time that they have to let them be the hero.<br /> <br /> - Legends exist of remedies for everything, including Banality, in he Deep Dreaming, so you could send your PCs to look for one such artifact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":5826,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","user":"monteparnas","date":".  bad coding 10-03-2021, 03:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-03T09:41:51-07:00","id":1462562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Froggy711</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1462451-how-might-a-group-of-mages-help-a-changeling-at-risk-of-being-undone-by-banality?p=1462459#post1462459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, assume we are talking about Arete 3 mages here. I am assuming this is going to be more than a &amp;quot;Roll arete to remove banality Effect&amp;quot; and probably involving the mages doing... something... to help? I am just not familiar enough with changeling to know how that all works.<br /> <br /> Mostly I found her an interesting character and wanted to see how to incorporate her into a mage chronicle, maybe as a one-off.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh! I thought it was Changeling PCs, sorry.<br /> <br /> I think the most interesting thing to have is the effects of the Mists on the PCs. That can really lead to some interesting moments, but you have to make sure your players are ok with their PCs forgetting some things that happened in game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-03T11:52:37-07:00","id":1462573,"title":"","content":"As Mages they can counter the Mists with Mind magic. Although it will be a thing at first, sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-03T14:14:23-07:00","id":1462591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1462451-how-might-a-group-of-mages-help-a-changeling-at-risk-of-being-undone-by-banality?p=1462573#post1462573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As Mages they can counter the Mists with Mind magic. Although it will be a thing at first, sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you remember enough to do it, and you're kind of screwed once your Mind effect has ended if you don't remember to do it again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-03T21:26:09-07:00","id":1462613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1462451-how-might-a-group-of-mages-help-a-changeling-at-risk-of-being-undone-by-banality?p=1462591#post1462591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you remember enough to do it, and you're kind of screwed once your Mind effect has ended if you don't remember to do it again.</div> </div> </div> </div>The average Traditionalist have Banality 4, some have 3. They'll remember enough. Making a permanent Mind effect to overcome this is also an issue. The ST can certainly use the Mists as a strong effect if this is the desired theme for the story, but this usually isn't the theme for Mage and they have ample resources to overcome it. It is a Mage game, not a Changeling game. Messing with their memory isn't at all necessary unless the ST and the players want to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-05T00:49:33-07:00","id":1462775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1462451-how-might-a-group-of-mages-help-a-changeling-at-risk-of-being-undone-by-banality?p=1462562#post1462562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh! I thought it was Changeling PCs, sorry.<br /> <br /> I think the most interesting thing to have is the effects of the Mists on the PCs. That can really lead to some interesting moments, but you have to make sure your players are ok with their PCs forgetting some things that happened in game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh, I assumed mages were immune to the mists, in the same way that Changelings don't count as witnesses to vulgar magick.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The average Traditionalist have Banality 4, some have 3. They'll remember enough. Making a permanent Mind effect to overcome this is also an issue. The ST can certainly use the Mists as a strong effect if this is the desired theme for the story, but this usually isn't the theme for Mage and they have ample resources to overcome it. It is a Mage game, not a Changeling game. Messing with their memory isn't at all necessary unless the ST and the players want to.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>I miiiight just ignore the mists, but then again, a mage with mind magick discovering that they have a strange gap in their memory about what they did last night, or that certain events have been &quot;smoothed over&quot; in their mind, is going to get their attention. I'll play that by ear, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-05T08:31:48-07:00","id":1462800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Froggy711</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1462451-how-might-a-group-of-mages-help-a-changeling-at-risk-of-being-undone-by-banality?p=1462775#post1462775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh, I assumed mages were immune to the mists, in the same way that Changelings don't count as witnesses to vulgar magick.</div> </div> </div> </div>No one is immune to the Mists, not even the Changelings themselves in fact as they are affected when they are even temporarily rendered Banal.<br /> <br /> But it doesn't have to be a specially strong effect. As low Banality Traditionalists your PCs are likely to have some recollections, as per the book:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><u>Banality 3</u><br /> <i>Disorientation:</i></b> The memory is jarring, strange, and may<br /> even set the mortal\u2019s head spinning \u2014 but something happened<br /> to her, and she knows it. She won\u2019t forget that it has happened,<br /> but she\u2019d be hard pressed to say just what exactly. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><u>Banality 4</u><br /> <i>Uncertain Memory:</i></b> The mortal remembers flashes,<br /> moments, and little more. She may doubt that what she\u2019s re-<br /> membering happened to her, but these memories had to come<br /> from somewhere. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><u>Banality 5</u><br /> <i>Hazy Memory:</i></b> The mortal can only grasp fleeting images<br /> from the incident she witnessed \u2014 the smell of autumn leaves, a<br /> brilliant blue flame, or the sound of strange laughter and music.<br /> Those sensory impressions stay with her, but she has no context<br /> for them whatsoever. Without physical evidence, she is likely<br /> to put it off as a strange reaction to food or drug, or perhaps a<br /> memory of a very strange and vivid dream. </div> </div> </div>Take the most open-minded or childish character and apply the first, to the most focused character apply the last, and the middle one to everyone else, then you'll have a nice spread of the Mists to grab their attention. The strange way this effect is spread among them and the fact that Willpower had no effect on it will help to deliver the themes of the story and get their curiosity at the same time.<br /> <br /> After that it isn't specially hard to fight the Mists. Any effect that can recall forgotten memories will do. Increasing mental acuity will fail, but that will also get them guessing, which is good. Recovering those memories in indirect ways, like taking notes or descriptions, will have lasting effects, while watching them complete will settle the Mists.<br /> <br /> Once they are Enchanted by the NPC to help with the problem the Mists will stay at bay until the effect wears off, which may take days and she can recharge. This will be a big investment from her, though, so you can have the Mists resettling and Mind magic following up from time to time if they can't finish it fast (which they probably can't). Nothing that their Magic or a few favors to other Changelings can't help with as any of them can also reinforce the Enchanted state.<br /> <br /> When your characters have learned enough about Glamour and Banality by completing some research you can let them have a lasting Mind effect as they low their own Banality for real. It is easier as it doesn't work as a disease on them, so just let the Mind effect to recollect perfectly be lasting. They can also self-Enchant with a point of Quintessence for 1 or a few days, but Enchanting always bring the problem of seeing and interacting with Chimerae all the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}